
DPMITEST - a 16-bit DPMI client
  real mode - is there a host?
    OK   1686h agrees we are not in protected mode
    OK   a host answered, with an entry point
         it reports DPMI 0.90
         32-bit clients: yes
  and into protected mode:
    OK   DOS still answers - printed by PM code
    OK   and CR0 says PE is set, so it really is
    OK   1686h agrees, the other way round now
  INT 31h - descriptors and memory:
    OK   the host reports version 0.90
    OK   selectors are 8 apart
    OK   a descriptor we built addresses what we said
    OK   4K of extended memory, written at both ends
    OK   and given back
  DOS, from protected mode:
    OK   30h answers with a version
    OK   a file written and read back, byte for byte
  0300h - a real-mode interrupt on our behalf:
and this line came out of real mode.
    OK   INT 21h ran in real mode and came back
  and a BIOS call, reflected:
    OK   INT 10h AH=0Fh answered
         it says the screen is 80
  0303h - and a callback, the other way about:
    OK   real mode called us, in protected mode
    OK   and the callback address freed
    OK   0305h: no state to save across a mode switch
  0300h INT 21h 4Bh - children, the way an extender starts them:
ARGS.COM - what a 16-bit program was handed:
  tail  [ 6]
  AX    0000
  FCB1  00 [6          ]
  FCB2  00 [           ]
  env   076B
    COMSPEC=C:\COMMAND.COM
    PATH=C:\TESTS;C:\
  path  C:\TESTS\ARGS.COM
    OK   a 16-bit child ran, and 4Dh says it exited 6
    OK   CMD.EXE ran through 0300h, over the bridge, and came back
  a child that ^C is about to end
    OK   a child ^C ended came back to us, and 4Dh says ^C
    OK   INT 33h from protected mode reached the mouse driver
DPMITEST done
